"cyp","2020/21;2021/22","fasbandf","Standard family-affluence comparisons are omitted for these years. An adjusted scale excluding holidays was used during the pandemic; it is not substituted for the standard scale here.","cyp_2023","Table 8: Family Affluence Scale"
"cyp","2019/20;2020/21;2021/22;2022/23;2023/24","disab_all_pop","The disability question was updated from 2019/20. Comparisons with earlier years should take the question change into account.","cyp_2019","Summary of changes / disability measure"
"cyp","2023/24","gend3","The Year 7-11 gender question wording changed in 2023/24, including a non-binary option and prefer-to-self-describe wording. The supplied grouped GEND3 dictionary still labels category 3 as Other; the pipeline preserves that grouped coding.","cyp_2023","1.2 School year 3-11 pupils and parents"
"cyp","2023/24","wt_gross","State and independent schools were weighted together for the first time in 2023/24. Use the supplied annual weight; a constant weight name does not imply an unchanged weighting method.","cyp_2023","4.1 Weighting pupil and parent data"
"cyp","all","wt_gross","This pipeline is configured for the supplied UK Data Service single-year main datasets, using wt_gross. It does not assume the wt_grossCCLA variable in the old scripts is an equivalent weight.","cyp_2023","3.2 Key variables; 4.1 Weighting pupil and parent data"
"adult","all","weights","Adult weights depend on the question and questionnaire group. Rows marked review in config/variables.csv are not analysed until their weight is checked; the imported data remain available.","adult_2023","Weighting, Table 5; consult each annual guide"
"adult","2016/17","volany","For 2016/17, Volint_ANY contains unlabelled valid codes 0 and 1. These were interpreted as No and Yes respectively, consistent with the labelled 2017/18 and 2018/19 files. This is an analyst assumption; the supplied 2016/17 documentation does not confirm these meanings. Negative missing/routing codes were excluded from the denominator.","adult_2016_volunteering_assumption","Analyst assumption approved for this report"
"adult","2016/17;2017/18;2018/19;2019/20;2020/21","readyab1_pop_gr2","Readiness was grouped as strongly agree versus other valid responses. Negative missing codes and any code 0 labelled 'Not asked' were excluded. Where respondents were skipped because they were already sufficiently active, estimates describe valid respondents to the question, not all adults. Comparisons with years using different routing require caution.","adult_readiness_processing","Grouping and eligible respondents"
"adult","2016/17;2017/18;2018/19","readyop1_pop_gr2","Readiness was grouped as strongly agree versus other valid responses. Negative missing codes and any code 0 labelled 'Not asked' were excluded. Where respondents were skipped because they were already sufficiently active, estimates describe valid respondents to the question, not all adults. Comparisons with years using different routing require caution.","adult_readiness_processing","Grouping and eligible respondents"
"adult","2017/18","wellb_anxious_gr","For 2017/18, anxiety categories were reconstructed from the original 0–10 score using the supplied category definitions: 0–1 very low, 2–3 low, 4–5 medium and 6–10 very high. Cross-tabulation showed that the supplied grouped variable did not consistently follow these boundaries. Negative missing codes were excluded. This is an analyst correction, not a revised data release.","adult_2017_anxiety_regrouping","Reconstruction of anxiety categories"
"adult","2017/18","wellb_happy_gr","For 2017/18, happiness categories were reconstructed from the original 0–10 score using the supplied category definitions: 0–4 low, 5–6 medium, 7–8 high and 9–10 very high. Cross-tabulation showed that the supplied grouped variable did not consistently follow these boundaries. Negative missing codes were excluded. This is an analyst correction, not a revised data release.","adult_2017_happiness_regrouping","Reconstruction of happiness categories"
"adult","2017/18","wellb_lifesat_gr","Life satisfaction categories for 2017/18 were reconstructed from the original 0–10 score using the supplied definitions: 0–4 low, 5–6 medium, 7–8 high and 9–10 very high. Cross-tabulation showed that the supplied grouped variable did not consistently follow these boundaries. Negative missing codes were excluded. This is an analyst correction, not a revised data release.","adult_2017_lifesat_regrouping","Reconstruction of wellbeing categories"
"adult","2017/18","wellb_worthw_gr","Worthwhile categories for 2017/18 were reconstructed from the original 0–10 score using the supplied definitions: 0–4 low, 5–6 medium, 7–8 high and 9–10 very high. Cross-tabulation showed that the supplied grouped variable did not consistently follow these boundaries. Negative missing codes were excluded. This is an analyst correction, not a revised data release.","adult_2017_worthw_regrouping","Reconstruction of wellbeing categories"
"adult","2016/17","readyab1_pop_gr2","Readiness was asked below the questionnaire-calculated 150-minute weekly activity threshold. Percentages describe eligible respondents with valid answers, not all adults. Routing exclusions and other missing responses are excluded. These estimates use wt_final_online; comparisons with years using broader question eligibility are not like-for-like.","adult_2016_online_questionnaire","Readiness routing and analysis denominator"
"adult","2017/18","readyab1_pop_gr2","Readiness was asked below the questionnaire-calculated 150-minute weekly activity threshold. Percentages describe eligible respondents with valid answers, not all adults. Routing exclusions and other missing responses are excluded. These estimates use wt_final_online; comparisons with years using broader question eligibility are not like-for-like.","adult_2017_online_questionnaire","Readiness routing and analysis denominator"
"adult","2017/18","readyab1_pop_gr2","Report-author-approved analytical decision: retain 20 valid responses labelled PAPER, all with positive supplied online weights. The reason for the mode discrepancy is unresolved; retention is not a confirmed Sport England instruction.","adult_2026_review_decisions","Mode discrepancy"
"adult","2016/17","readyop1_pop_gr2","Readiness was asked below the questionnaire-calculated 150-minute weekly activity threshold. Percentages describe eligible respondents with valid answers, not all adults. Routing exclusions and other missing responses are excluded. These estimates use wt_final_online; comparisons with years using broader question eligibility are not like-for-like.","adult_2016_online_questionnaire","Readiness routing and analysis denominator"
"adult","2017/18","readyop1_pop_gr2","Readiness was asked below the questionnaire-calculated 150-minute weekly activity threshold. Percentages describe eligible respondents with valid answers, not all adults. Routing exclusions and other missing responses are excluded. These estimates use wt_final_online; comparisons with years using broader question eligibility are not like-for-like.","adult_2017_online_questionnaire","Readiness routing and analysis denominator"
"adult","2017/18","readyop1_pop_gr2","Report-author-approved analytical decision: retain 20 valid responses labelled PAPER, all with positive supplied online weights. The reason for the mode discrepancy is unresolved; retention is not a confirmed Sport England instruction.","adult_2026_review_decisions","Mode discrepancy"
"adult","2016/17;2017/18;2018/19;2019/20;2020/21;2021/22;2022/23","motive_pop_gr2","Percentages describe strong agreement among eligible respondents with valid answers to item E, not among all adults. The reviewed questionnaires ask E only after neutral/disagree/strongly disagree responses to all preceding motivation items A-D. Respondents not asked and other missing responses are excluded, not counted as disagreeing. Analysis uses wt_final_online. This conditional denominator is the analytical approach adopted for this report.","adult_2026_review_decisions","Conditional motivation denominator"
"adult","2016/17","motive_pop_gr2","The questionnaire routes item E on both the sport and exercise branches to respondents selecting response 3, 4 or 5 on each of A-D.","adult_2016_online_questionnaire","Motivation routing"
"adult","2017/18","motive_pop_gr2","The questionnaire routes item E on both the sport and exercise branches to respondents selecting response 3, 4 or 5 on each of A-D.","adult_2017_online_questionnaire","Motivation routing"
"adult","2017/18","motive_pop_gr2","Analytical decision: retain eight valid PAPER-labelled responses with positive supplied online weights, following the report-author-approved approach to the readiness mode discrepancy. Their origin remains unresolved.","adult_2026_review_decisions","Mode discrepancy"
"adult","2020/21","lone","2020/21 loneliness estimates are temporarily omitted. The Year 6 User Guide specifies wt_lone, but that weight was not found in the directly shared dataset. The appropriate weight for this file remains unresolved.","adult_2020","Weighting, Table 5; supplied-file weight inventory"
"adult","2018/19","lone","2018/19 loneliness uses wt_final_C, the online group 2 weight, as specified in the Year 4 User Guide, Table 6. All 52,502 valid responses in the supplied file are online and have positive values for this weight. Percentages exclude routing exclusions and other missing responses.","adult_2018","Weighting, Table 6; supplied-file response coverage"
